  "// archetypes": "Normalization runs once or twice per transformer block, on the same activation tensor the block's matmuls produce -- so its shapes are the model's hidden width against however many tokens are in flight, not arbitrary three-dimensional boxes.",
  "// neighbourhood": "hidden_dim is absent from the neighbourhood: it is fixed by the model architecture and takes a handful of values, so an interpolated 5000 is a width nobody ships. batch and seq_len are what actually vary between requests.",
  "// elements": "in + out, plus the scale vector. No bias, unlike layernorm. Element count across every tensor the operation touches, inputs and outputs. Dtype-free on purpose: bytes is elements times the dtype width, and the width table belongs to the tool rather than repeated as a nested dtype lookup in seven declarations. gbs = bytes / measured time, which is the metric that ranks a memory-bound kernel where tflops cannot.",
